Dual License Declaration
------------------------
The Tickraft software (the "Software") is distributed under a dual
license model. You may choose to use the Software under either of the
following licenses:

  1. GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPLv3)
  2. Tickraft Commercial License

License Selection Rules
-----------------------
- AGPLv3 applies by default: Any user that has not signed a commercial
  license agreement with the copyright holder is automatically subject
  to the terms of AGPLv3.
- Commercial license requires a separate agreement: To waive the
  obligations imposed by AGPLv3, you must contact the copyright holder
  to sign a commercial license agreement, after which the Tickraft
  Commercial License will apply to you.

Application Guide
-----------------
- Open-source users (including individuals, community members, and
  open-source projects): AGPLv3 applies by default. Derivative works
  and network services based on the Software must be released under
  AGPLv3.
- Commercial users (including enterprises with private deployments and
  SaaS providers): A commercial license agreement must be signed to
  waive AGPLv3 obligations, allowing closed-source distribution of
  derivative works and the provision of network services without
  source disclosure.

